{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8295c69207808d7b45acba3e72a5825152106b5efb306553878b66565613be80", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThus we define the corresponding standard coverings of affines as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c6fc6acd5442ae08d942785456938b46f7474665c094eb74d77f623a49f76092", "unit_id": "tag:0214:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{f_j : U_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0004": "$U_j$", "MATH_0005": "$T$", "MATH_0006": "$T = \\bigcup f_j(U_j)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-standard-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7d2706466bb0058bd4dd583aed6befd574271a106036ff6e165ae642030d1604", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5a0638e82b89fb8bdbac7fb3501134008a59cbd7a60297da75d3b110f04ebc6f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>standard <ACCENT_0001>tale covering<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nof <MATH_0002> is a family <MATH_0003>\nwith each <MATH_0004> is affine and <ACCENT_0002>tale over <MATH_0005> and\n<MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:14ad73b64f9fdcc5ff0d7b4beb8cad7923ef6f330fd794478ef4086a16e113b2", "unit_id": "tag:0219:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f_j$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{Aff}/S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-standard-etale}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-etale-standard-smooth}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTBFCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTBFOPEN_0001": "{\\bf "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bacaf8951af335b89080cfa2ba40c7c0794384d8651813c069605fa2a977fa76", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a681ef8651629db3683f4dd0360f4f3eecc64da61ddc7e47ba04fef86afda3c9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the definition above we do <TEXTBFOPEN_0001>not<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> assume the morphisms <MATH_0001> are\nstandard <ACCENT_0001>tale. The reason is that if we did then the standard <ACCENT_0002>tale\ncoverings would not define a site on <MATH_0002>, for example because of\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001> part (4).\nOn the other hand, an <ACCENT_0003>tale morphism of affines is automatically\nstandard smooth, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nHence a standard <ACCENT_0004>tale covering is a standard smooth\ncovering and a standard syntomic covering.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f9c15f6c93385d8d1e8d852fd38f5043f01e96e70ad89a651a99984f13d25c91", "unit_id": "tag:0214:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\Sch_\\etale$", "MATH_0002": "$S_0$", "MATH_0003": "$\\text{Cov}_0$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sch_\\alpha$", "MATH_0005": "$S_0$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sch_\\alpha$", "MATH_0007": "$\\text{Cov}_0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sets-lemma-construct-category}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sets-lemma-coverings-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-big-etale-site}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:20878f4b03b59bf24a79ccd26bb2fb0689b8e0ecc3ae99814688ee8f6ffbd63e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7641449f8c82c3674e7b5d429766f8f27bc149c76096c28f6d5b3177a1d05938", "source_text": "A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>big <ACCENT_0001>tale site<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is any site <MATH_0001> as in\nSites, Definition <REF_0001> constructed as follows:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Choose any set of schemes <MATH_0002>, and any set of <ACCENT_0002>tale coverings\n<MATH_0003> among these schemes.\n<STRUCT_0003> As underlying category take any category <MATH_0004>\nconstructed as in Sets, Lemma <REF_0002>\nstarting with the set <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0004> Choose any set of coverings as in\nSets, Lemma <REF_0003> starting with the\ncategory <MATH_0006> and the class of <ACCENT_0003>tale coverings,\nand the set <MATH_0007> chosen above.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:49337b0f2ea11a24d66dae6836a323dbf66d3c09a518fe3950aa82241100b459", "unit_id": "tag:021A:statement"}
